    "description": "• Led design and implementation of a real-time worker-presence detection system for a safety-critical roadway broadcast platform — introduced a multi-table DynamoDB architecture (live state, immutable version history, signed broadcast artifacts, raw observations) enabling complete historical reconstruction of broadcast activity, and refactored the MQTT publisher from direct command-handling to reconcile-from-state semantics, improving resilience.\n• Designed the highly scalable, event-driven SQS/MQTT ingestion pipeline for the worker-presence system: idempotent observation writes, deterministic deduplication across overlapping geofences, conditional state expiry, and DLQ-based failure handling — with safety-critical base broadcasts isolated from advisory pipeline failures.\n• Designed and implemented a serverless Node.js backend on AWS (Lambda, API Gateway, DocumentDB) for automotive manufacturing certificate issuance, integrating factory-deployed hardware with external PKI partner systems across a multi-step enrollment, ACK/NACK, and cross-system state synchronization workflow.\n• Owned cloud-side certificate lifecycle logic for a new regional SCMS deployment, including enrollment event ingestion, successor enrollment, and cross-system state synchronization with a regional PKI partner.\n• Designed and implemented a multi-region device registration system across North America and Europe, enforcing global uniqueness of device identity across distributed factory sources by detecting serial-number and public-key collisions beyond local hardware constraints.\n• Contributed to a production hybrid-cloud platform (SCMS) serving tens of thousands of connected vehicle and traffic infrastructure devices, working across Node.js services, AWS (Lambda, ECS, SQS, DynamoDB, DocumentDB, Redis), and HSM-backed cryptographic operations.\n• Improved CI scalability by containerizing system test environments and enabling parallel Jenkins execution, increasing test throughput.",
